        "content" : {
          "size" : 7797,
          "compression" : 0,
          "mimeType" : "text/html; charset=utf-8",
          "text" : "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html>\n<!--LAB_HEAD_START-->\n    <head>\n        <link href=/resources/labheader/css/academyLabHeader.css rel=stylesheet>\n        <link href=/resources/css/labsBlog.css rel=stylesheet>\n        <title>Password reset broken logic</title>\n    </head>\n<!--LAB_HEAD_END-->\n    <body>\n        <script src=\"/resources/labheader/js/labHeader.js\"></script>\n        <!--LAB_HEADER_START-->\n        <div id=\"academyLabHeader\">\n            <section class='academyLabBanner'>\n                <div class=container>\n                    <div class=logo></div>\n                        <div class=title-container>\n                            <h2>Password reset broken logic</h2>\n                            <a id='exploit-link' class='button' target='_blank' href='https://exploit-0aa4002a047f298d801e8e9f017b00de.exploit-server.net/email'>Email client</a>\n                            <a class=link-back href='https://portswigger.net/web-security/authentication/other-mechanisms/lab-password-reset-broken-logic'>\n                                Back&nbsp;to&nbsp;lab&nbsp;description&nbsp;\n                                <svg version=1.1 id=Layer_1 xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' xmlns:xlink='http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink' x=0px y=0px viewBox='0 0 28 30' enable-background='new 0 0 28 30' xml:space=preserve title=back-arrow>\n                                    <g>\n                                        <polygon points='1.4,0 0,1.2 12.6,15 0,28.8 1.4,30 15.1,15'></polygon>\n                                        <polygon points='14.3,0 12.9,1.2 25.6,15 12.9,28.8 14.3,30 28,15'></polygon>\n                                    </g>\n                                </svg>\n                            </a>\n                        </div>\n                        <div class='widgetcontainer-lab-status is-notsolved'>\n                            <span>LAB</span>\n                            <p>Not solved</p>\n                            <span class=lab-status-icon></span>\n                        </div>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n        </div>\n        <!--LAB_HEADER_END-->\n        <div theme=\"blog\">\n            <section class=\"maincontainer\">\n                <div class=\"container is-page\">\n                    <header class=\"navigation-header\">\n                        <section class=\"top-links\">\n                            <a href=/>Home</a><p>|</p>\n                            <a href=\"/my-account?id=wiener\">My account</a><p>|</p>\n                        </section>\n                    </header>\n                    <header class=\"notification-header\">\n                    </header>\n                    <div class=\"blog-post\">\n                    <img src=\"/image/blog/posts/48.jpg\">\n                    <h1>Look No Hands - The Game Plays Itself</h1>\n                    <p><span id=blog-author>Mike Pleasure</span> | 21 January 2026</p>\n                    <hr>\n                    <p>I was so fed up with my husband always sitting in front of the television playing his silly games, I did something about it. I came up with an idea that would revolutionize game playing in the future. I wrote letters to the top game designers with my idea. I was surprised and delighted by the positive response.</p>\n                    <p>Eventually, we received the prototype game in the post. This was the first ever self-playing video game. No more endless button bashing. No more arguments trying to get him out of his Barcalounger so he could help me with cooking dinner. His hands were finally free to do all the things I needed him to do.</p>\n                    <p>Before the game begins you have to take a personality test, this then creates an algorithm for gameplay. The game then becomes intuitive, running along making choices for the player, all he had to do was watch with his eyes, and keep his hands free for more important jobs. My husband&apos;s temper improved dramatically as he didn&apos;t have to repeat levels with angry button pressing, they repeated automatically.</p>\n                    <p>The game is so realistic, lives will be lost if it thinks you could have made the wrong choices. Based on the results of your personality test the game leads you along paths it is certain you would choose. The accuracy was astonishing. My husband even agreed they had worked him out a lot quicker than I did.</p>\n                    <p>When this goes to market I&apos;m pretty sure I&apos;ll be in the running for the Nobel peace prize. If it was based on votes from women I would win for sure. I can&apos;t understand how I could be the first to come up with this idea. It makes perfect sense to me. Now to invent something that gets him to put his laundry in the hamper.</p>\n                    <div/>\n                    <hr>\n                    <h1>Comments</h1>\n                    <section class=\"comment\">\n                        <p>\n                        <img src=\"/resources/images/avatarDefault.svg\" class=\"avatar\">                            Brian Side | 23 January 2026\n                        </p>\n                        <p>I&apos;m hiding in the shed reading this. My wife will never find me. Mostly because we don&apos;t have a shed and I&apos;m in a furniture store.</p>\n                        <p></p>\n                    </section>\n                    <section class=\"comment\">\n                        <p>\n                        <img src=\"/resources/images/avatarDefault.svg\" class=\"avatar\">                            Allyoucan Pete | 30 January 2026\n                        </p>\n                        <p>Don&apos;t give up your day job.</p>\n                        <p></p>\n                    </section>\n                    <section class=\"comment\">\n                        <p>\n                        <img src=\"/resources/images/avatarDefault.svg\" class=\"avatar\">                            Wendy House | 05 February 2026\n                        </p>\n                        <p>That&apos;s the most fun I&apos;ve had reading since I had to do a speech dressed as a clown.</p>\n                        <p></p>\n                    </section>\n                    <section class=\"comment\">\n                        <p>\n                        <img src=\"/resources/images/avatarDefault.svg\" class=\"avatar\">                            Fred Time | 10 February 2026\n                        </p>\n                        <p>Will you marry me?</p>\n                        <p></p>\n                    </section>\n                    <hr>\n                    <section class=\"add-comment\">\n                        <h2>Leave a comment</h2>\n                        <form action=\"/post/comment\" method=\"POST\" enctype=\"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\">\n                            <input required type=\"hidden\" name=\"postId\" value=\"4\">\n                            <label>Comment:</label>\n                            <textarea required rows=\"12\" cols=\"300\" name=\"comment\"></textarea>\n                                    <label>Name:</label>\n                                    <input required type=\"text\" name=\"name\">\n                                    <label>Email:</label>\n                                    <input required type=\"email\" name=\"email\">\n                                    <label>Website:</label>\n                                    <input pattern=\"(http:|https:).+\" type=\"text\" name=\"website\">\n                            <button class=\"button\" type=\"submit\">Post Comment</button>\n                        </form>\n                    </section>\n                    <div class=\"is-linkback\">\n                        <a href=\"/\">Back to Blog</a>\n                    </div>\n                </div>\n            </section>\n            <div class=\"footer-wrapper\">\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </body>\n</html>\n"
